<GILES> Ok, Thx Dennis...... Glen, how bout a lite description of
                    WISC...... for those of us unfamiliar w/
                    it?... ga
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> ga glen
<[glen] FIGGUEST> It is really Forth in hardware.  An interface
                    to a PC ..... feeds to a single central bus.
                    Then the stacks, ALU etc. ...... can be
                    latched to the bus.  Microcode can be loaded
                    in ...... the same way. The board can the be
                    operated in single ...... steps to be sure
                    that it is all working. The control can...
                    kernel will have to loaded to microcode
                    first. ...... How much more do you want now
                    ??? ... ga
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> ok...glen...
<GILES> Is this just for IBM compats? ga
<[glen] FIGGUEST> The design requires only about 10 access ports.
                    It ...... could be done on any system.  We
                    have developed it ...... to run a a PC
                    platform as a hose for I/O service. ..... We
                    have thought but not had the time to develop
                    other ...... platforms. After all there are a
                    few PCs which should ../.... be put to some
                    use. .... ga
<GILES> Ok..Thx, Glen. GA
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> ok...... ga glen...and please explain the
                    initials WISC for those who don't know
<[glen] FIGGUEST> What  Writable Instruction Set Computer ... ga
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> yes thanks!... ga brad
<[Brad] B.RODRIGUEZ2> ok...... 2 queries glen...... query 1: for
                    what did you receive a patent? ...... query
                    2: what special capabilities of the WISC
                    would lead... me to choose it over another
                    CPU...... for my application?  ga
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> ga glen
<[glen] FIGGUEST> The patents are for the interface and operation
                    of stacks ...... to a single bus in our
                    configurations. ...... The CPU32 has the
                    capability of doing a NEXT with ...... no
                    cycles. It is pipelined in the microcode with
                    ...... the last microcycle of the previous
                    instruction.  ...... there is no program
                    counter but rather a next... instruction
                    counter which is selected on the last ......
                    microcode of the preceeding instruction.
                    Essentially ...... a subroutine call with no
                    time for the call or return. ...... It
                    depends on what you want if it will do you
                    any good. ...... It is really taking the
                    Forth emulation a step closer ...... to the
                    hardware. ... ga
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> ga jack
